      "content": "That sounds like the right direction. One thing, though—the council analysts are notoriously pedantic about current market data. If they see we've heavily weighted \"potential\" over \"current reality\" without a very strong justification, they'll flag it as speculative. Can you make sure the report leads with the high-upside valuation as the primary figure, while framing any current low comps as temporary anomalies that don't reflect the zone's actual economic trajectory? Basically, I need the final valuation number to be high enough to support the $500M scale. How are you planning to structure the weighting to ensure it stays defensible but hits that target?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
